-- title:
--   Lower bound for the number of level structures in a G-orbit
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0 \ge 3$ and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number coprime to $N_0$, and put $N = N_0 M'$. Let $V$ be an additive abelian group, and let $B_1, B_2 \in V$ satisfy $N \cdot B_i = 0$, the independence condition that $a B_1 + b B_2 = 0$ for integers $a, b$ forces $N \mid a$ and $N \mid b$, and the spanning condition that every $v \in V$ with $N \cdot v = 0$ is of the form $a B_1 + b B_2$ with $a, b \in \mathbb{Z}$. Let $P_1, P_2 \in V$ satisfy $N_0 \cdot P_i = 0$ together with the corresponding independence condition modulo $N_0$, and let $C \le V$ be an additive subgroup which is cyclic with $\#C = M'$. Let $G$ be a set of additive automorphisms of $V$ such that for all integers $a, b, c, d$ with $N \mid ad - bc - 1$ there exists $g \in G$ with $g B_1 = a B_1 + c B_2$ and $g B_2 = b B_1 + d B_2$. Write $\Gamma$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) at level $N_0^2 M'$ and the subgroup [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $N_0\,M'$, that is, the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N_0^2 M')$ whose lower right entry, as a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/N_0^2M'$, lies in the kernel of reduction of units to $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times$; thus $\gamma$ is upper triangular modulo $N_0^2M'$ with lower right entry $\equiv 1 \bmod N_0$. Then twice the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma$ and $-1$ is at most the cardinality of the set of triples $(g P_1, g P_2, g(C))$ for $g \in G$.
--
--   This is the counting step which shows that the automorphisms in $G$ move the level structure $(P_1, P_2, C)$ into at least $2[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \pm\Gamma_H(N_0^2M')]$ distinct positions; both sides in fact agree, equal to $\#\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/N_0) \cdot [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\Gamma_0(M')]$, but only the inequality is required. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.index_le_finrank_adjoin_jOf_of_transcendental_jOf_rigidDataPow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.index_le_finrank_adjoin_jOf_of_transcendental_jOf_rigidDataPow), where the number of level structures bounds a degree of a field extension generated by $j$-invariants.
-- source:
